## Review & Understand the Task

- The Git screen **already exists**: `src/components/repo/GitView.vue` (full screen: toolbar, fetch/pull/push, branch list, commits, commit & merge modals, `ChangesPanel` for diffs).
- It is **already registered** in `src/config/appComponentsMap.js` as `'git-view'`, and `src/views/infra/InfraView.vue` is registered as `'infra'` — so no component/map work is needed (and the previously proposed `src/views/GitView.vue` must **not** be created; it would be a duplicate).
- What is actually missing is **routing**. On mobile / single mode an app click goes `NavItem → $ui.setActiveTab(key) → navigation.openApp → $router.push(def.route())`. `config/apps.js` declares routes for `activity` and `git-view`, but `src/router/index.ts` registers **no route with those names** → `$router.push({ name: 'activity' | 'git-view' })` fails and the click does nothing (silently).
- The mobile home redirect in `router/navigate.js` also targets `{ name: 'activity' }`, so it hit the same dead route.

## Information Gathered

| App key (`config/apps.js`) | Route declared | Exists in `router/index.ts` | Component in `appComponentsMap.js` | Mobile result before |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `activity` | `{ name: 'activity' }` | ❌ **missing** | ✅ `components/wall/Wall.vue` | nothing happens |
| `git-view` | `{ name: 'git-view' }` | ❌ **missing** | ✅ `components/repo/GitView.vue` | nothing happens |
| `infra` | `{ name: 'infra' }` | ✅ | ✅ `views/infra/InfraView.vue` | works |
| tasks / planning / messenger / meet / team / file-explorer / wiki / workspaces / docs / knowledge / settings / account / logs / metrics / analytics / team-* / vibe-coding | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | works |

Cross-check of **every** route name in `config/apps.js` against `router/index.ts`: the only two unmatched names are `activity` and `git-view`.

## Changes Summary

